{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/622763-going-borg-on-banes","id":622763,"title":"Going Borg on Banes?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-10T16:04:52-07:00","id":622763,"title":"Going Borg on Banes?","content":"The Wyrm cannot truly create, or so I understand. It instead merely corrupts, so a lot of spirits that were once pure and helpful to the Garou are now their worst nightmares. But what about the Weaver? We've seen what it does to humans, transforming them into drones. It seems that subverting a beings will and assimilating it should be something that the Weaver should be able to manage. I remember reading about how a lot of Hunter Spiders have been corrupted. What about Ferociti, Dream Makers, and even Nexus Crawlers that have been assimilated?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T18:16:47-07:00","id":622968,"title":"","content":"I don't entirely agree with the core logic here: that the Wyrm cannot create spirits, it can only corrupt them. There are plenty of spirits that are, and always have been, Wyrm spirits.<br /> <br /> That being said, there should be a Weaver version of the same &quot;corrupting&quot; influence. I think a Weaver subverted Nexus Crawler would be unlikely, given the Nexus Crawler's core nature, but it could make for an interesting unique encounter/antagonist. A lot of the top tier Spirits (like Nexus Crawlers) are really hard to picture &quot;corrupted&quot; in any form other than what they are already. I cant remember the name of the Wyld equivalent of a Nexus Cralwer, but they have a similar charm (Break Reality instead of Warp Reality) and I don't see them ending up as Wyrm or Weaver spirits ever. Just my opinion on that though.<br /> On the other hand, it is much more likely for the Weaver to simply lock away a spirit like that instead of converting it. Such is the nature of the Weaver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T22:56:07-07:00","id":623138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/622763-going-borg-on-banes?p=622968#post622968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't entirely agree with the core logic here: that the Wyrm cannot create spirits, it can only corrupt them. There are plenty of spirits that are, and always have been, Wyrm spirits.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Aha!!! I keep remembering rules and facts of the WOD game and people think I am nuts! But I just found the time to go through the books and I have the book and page that proves I am right!<br /> <br /> Book of the Wyrm Revised, pg. 42, &quot;This Fount and others like it are the closest the Wyrm can ever come to the act of creation. Through this fount, the Wyrm can &quot;create&quot; Banes and even other, more powerful minions. The Wyld is the source of the actual creative energy, but here, all that is created is turned to the Wyrm's control and power.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Font was the Font of Dark Possibilities that uses a HUGE Vortex as its wellspring. And now for my next trick, I am going to prove that mortals got a Willpower roll to resist the Embrace in one of the past editions.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And the Weaver is also totally a being that wants to give everything its own place. Sometimes that place is in a web, sometimes that place is helping to create the Web.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 08-11-2015, 03:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T07:53:17-07:00","id":628634,"title":"","content":"Not all Wyrm Spirits are Banes. Banes are (mostly) corrupt spirits, though. Actual conceptio and Creation of spirits is an iffy thing in the WoD, as they come to being from the need of a greater spirit for servants, from free agents chosing a side and becoming more or less a part of it to actual human dreams, desires and emotions actually creating things in the Umbra. This spiritogenesis is unrelated to the core principles that the Triat represents and functions with or without their influence. Do you honestly believe that the three principles of existence would ever lack for servants or would be unable to create them on a whim?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}